Z||000000||87FieroGTx||11-14-2001||07:01 PM|||| Why don't more people do the 3.5 TDC It's a all aluminum 24 valve multi cam V6!<P> Is it unreliable? Expensive?<P> It weighs the same as the I4 Duke so handling would be much beter than any other swap other than a Quad 4, <P> It has 215hp 230tq stock (Maybe WCF Turbo would fit, They made 350hp from the 3.4 TDC I don't see why you couldn't do something similar to this one)  and is said to be a MEAN sounding engine.<P> 215hp 230tq!<BR> Low weight!<BR> Great sound!<P><BR> I may consider this swap! <P> Oh is this the engine people call the Short Star?||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||11-14-2001||07:04 PM||||Ummm... I was going to ask if that was the "shortstar".  If so, then the engineering required to install one would be the same amount of work/effort required to install a Northstar engine.<P>It's like someone buying an Archie V8 kit and using it to install their 4.3L Vortech V6...why the time & effort for the lesser power rating?<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
